  "description": "Nitration of cellulose (cotton linters or wood pulp) with mixed acid to produce nitrocellulose (guncotton) and pyroxylin. Includes manufacture of single-base and double-base smokeless powders via gelatinization, extrusion, and drying. Foundation of the smokeless powder industry and early plastics (celluloid).",
